{"name":"Tea Light","hex":"#f8e4c2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tea light","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of tealight."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea_light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tealight","blocks":[{"text":"A tealight is a candle contained in a thin metal or plastic cup so that its wax can melt completely while lit. They are typically small, circular, usually wider than their height, and inexpensive. Tealights derive their name from their use in teapot warmers, but are also used as food warmers in general, e.g. fondue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Waxinelicht_-_aangestoken_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Waxinelicht_-_aangestoken_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tealight"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tealight%21.jpg/500px-Tealight%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tealight%21.jpg/1280px-Tealight%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tealight%21.jpg/500px-Tealight%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A tealight warming a teapot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATealight!.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Heilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG/500px-Heilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Heilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG/1280px-Heilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Heilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG/500px-Heilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Advent labyrinth made with 2,500 burning tealights at the Holy Cross – Centre for Christian Meditation and Spirituality, Bornheim, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeilig_Kreuz_Kerzenlabyrinth_15122012_02.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Heart-shaped_tea-light_candle_holder%2C_Himalayan_salt.jpg/500px-Heart-shaped_tea-light_candle_holder%2C_Himalayan_salt.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki